"Demons plague Artona I, the Artonan mother planet, and some resource worlds."
"The demon problem is only more or less contained."
"Avowed get thrown in front of demon disasters."
"Consorting with demons is a pastime of extremely powerful Artonans."
"Wealthy Artonans pay labs to contain demonic energies."
"Humans know demons as chaos-tainted Very Bad Monsters."
"A demon swarm is black dots like big carpenter bees that fly drunkenly."
"Swarm fragments pass through metal, leaving tiny holes, and knock out teleport runes."
"A fragment striking a preserved item strains the preserving skill hard."
"Earth's demon fight is held at Matadero, the offshore 'Slaughterhouse' near Anesidora."
"Official Demon Day is likely a fake date; the real one is announced once the fight is over."
"Demons break through as incursives, oozing chaos, at the spot where such things break through."
"A slain demon can crack apart at its seams, its remains shattering like glass."
"Chaos is felt as tension, sickness and an unwanted gaze, lingering after the demon dies."
"Wizards can fall and become demons; an origin demon may once have been a wizard."
"Breakthroughs led by an intelligence are the most dangerous kind."
"Demons prone to remaining have stubborn drives; one obsessed with minds made a planet a mind snare."
